      "writtenOn": "2021-01-05T05:33:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Daejun,\n\nI am testing the HPB changes on one of our stable Android R builds, but I see filesystem corruption several times (no power loss happened at all during my test). The corruption still happens even after I do a factory reset (I only enabled HPB on LU0 and it is where I mount the user data partition. I have not enable any pinned regions, I only have wLUMaxActiveHPBRegions as 4096 as of now).  I have tried with different UFS3.1 parts from different flash vendors, but I see filesystem corruption regardless of the UFS parts. Is there anything special that I need to pay attention to? Like provision or something?\n\nI am using version #12. I will back port version #18 and give it try again.\n\nThanks,\nCan Guo.",
      "revId": "9c40d54cfc5dac7e3edcb1019bb189fef0d5525d",
